In .NET 10 (and late .NET 9), Android deprecated `SOFT_INPUT_ADJUST_RESIZE` at the platform level, so `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` no longer works. MAUI now includes **`KeyboardAutoManagerScroll`** which is enabled by default — but it works best with `ScrollView` content, not fixed bottom bars.

For a chat screen with a pinned input bar, here's the recommended approach:

## Option 1: Use Android window insets (recommended)

In `Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs`:

```csharp
using Android.Views;
using AndroidX.Core.View;

protected override void OnCreate(Bundle? savedInstanceState)
{
    base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);

    // Ensure adjustResize-like behavior via insets
    WindowCompat.SetDecorFitsSystemWindows(Window!, false);

    ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(Window!.DecorView, new InsetsListener());
}

private class InsetsListener : Java.Lang.Object, IOnApplyWindowInsetsListener
{
    public WindowInsetsCompat OnApplyWindowInsets(Android.Views.View v, WindowInsetsCompat insets)
    {
        var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
        var systemInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.SystemBars());

        v.SetPadding(
            systemInsets.Left,
            systemInsets.Top,
            systemInsets.Right,
            Math.Max(imeInsets.Bottom, systemInsets.Bottom));

        return insets;
    }
}
```

## Option 2: Disable auto-scroll and set soft input mode in manifest

In `Platforms/Android/AndroidManifest.xml`, set:
```xml
<activity android:windowSoftInputMode="adjustResize" ... />
```

Then disable MAUI's auto-scroll for your page (it can conflict):
```csharp
#if ANDROID
KeyboardAutoManagerScroll.Disconnect();
#endif
```

Call `KeyboardAutoManagerScroll.Connect()` when navigating away if other pages need it.

## Layout tip

Structure your chat page so the input bar is outside the scrollable area:

```xml
<Grid RowDefinitions="*,Auto">
    <CollectionView Grid.Row="0" ItemsSource="{Binding Messages}" />
    <Entry Grid.Row="1" Placeholder="Type a message..." />
</Grid>
```

**Option 1** is the most robust for .NET 10 since it uses the modern WindowInsets API that replaced the deprecated resize mode.
